    31	
    32	**What the simulator does:** calculate truck events, empty and loaded travel, queues, loading/unloading, fuel bookkeeping, preventive repairs and configurable disruptions with reproducible seeds. It publishes hypothetical truck attributes through the real Eclipse Ditto MQTT channel, where twins can be read back. It never claims actual mine deliveries, measured fuel or observed equipment failures.
    33	
    34	**Important physical/model limitations:** Each route is a directed segment, not detailed turn-by-turn geometry. Existing routes may be long; slope proxies are *not derived* from the schematic x/y map. A fault starts at the next safe discrete-event boundary for moving trucks. Previously started operations may finish. Material is labeled generic hauled rock/ore; no proven geological grade, crusher throughput physics, blending or processing recovery. Fuel is estimated from class rates instead of engine load curves. Fleet comparisons are synthetic.
    35	
    36	**Quality protocol:** Compare dispatch strategies with *identical seed, equipment, event assumptions and duration*. Compare disruptions against a normal run with the same strategy and seed. Check litres/tonne and tonnes/day together—lower total litres by producing fewer tonnes is not a win. Repeat tests across multiple independent deterministic seeds and disclose counterintuitive scenario results instead of forcing a positive benefit.
